   {
    "eyebrow": "Naming, explained",
    "h2": "Is Dell Precision discontinued? The 2025&ndash;2026 naming story",
    "html": "<p>Short answer: the <em>name</em> has been through the wringer; the machines and our service for them carry on regardless.</p><p>In January 2025 Dell retired the 32-year-old Precision brand as part of a sweeping rename, and new workstations shipped for a while badged &ldquo;Dell Pro Max&rdquo;. Then at CES in January 2026 Dell announced further changes to its workstation naming for 2026 models. Because Dell has now changed course twice in twelve months, we&rsquo;d rather not carve the current official name into this page &mdash; check dell.com for whatever the badge says this quarter.</p><p>What matters to you is simpler: virtually every workstation in service in Dorset today is badged <strong>Precision</strong>, people still search for &ldquo;Precision&rdquo;, and we repair, upgrade and support all of them &mdash; along with the 2025 Pro Max interlude machines and whatever Dell calls their successors. Same silicon philosophy, same serviceable design, same jobs on our bench. And if you need a brand-new workstation, we order it to spec through our Dell reseller account under whichever name Dell is using that week.</p>"
   },
   {
    "eyebrow": "Windows 10 &amp; keeping them dependable",
    "h2": "Windows 10 has ended &mdash; and how we keep working workstations working",
    "html": "<p>Windows 10 support ended on 14 October 2025. A Precision still running it today is receiving no security updates unless it&rsquo;s enrolled in Microsoft&rsquo;s Extended Security Updates &mdash; and ESU itself ends on 13 October 2026, so it&rsquo;s a bridge, not a destination. Most recent Precisions upgrade to Windows 11 cleanly; we check your exact model against Dell&rsquo;s tested list before touching anything. Our guides on <a href=\"/windows-10-esu-or-upgrade-your-dell/\">ESU versus upgrading your Dell</a> and <a href=\"/dell-this-pc-cant-run-windows-11/\">what to do when a Dell can&rsquo;t run Windows 11</a> walk through the options honestly.</p><p>For businesses that depend on these machines daily, the better answer than firefighting is a support plan. Our <a href=\"/business-it-support-plans/\">business IT support plans</a> start from &pound;24.38 per computer per month and include a full service every six weeks with a written Service Report left on the Desktop &mdash; proof of what was checked and done, not promises. You also get the touches our customers actually tell us they value: we call before we connect remotely, and you deal with the same faces every time, not a rotating helpdesk. Microsoft 365 management is &pound;4.85 per user per month alongside. Dell-specific detail lives on our <a href=\"/dell-support-plans/\">Dell support plans</a> page, and the wider picture on our <a href=\"/dell-it-support-dorset/\">Dell IT support for Dorset</a> hub.</p><p>Support is Monday to Friday, 9&ndash;5, with same-day response &mdash; we won&rsquo;t pretend to be a 24/7 operation, because we aren&rsquo;t one.</p>"
   },
   {
    "eyebrow": "Replacement, truthfully",
    "h2": "When a Precision really is finished",
    "html": "<p>Sometimes the honest advice is that the repair money would be wasted. When that day comes, here is exactly what we can and can&rsquo;t offer &mdash; because pretending otherwise helps nobody.</p><p><strong>We do not stock Precision workstations, new or refurbished.</strong> Our refurbished stock is business-grade Dell <a href=\"/dell-hardware/#pick\">Latitude laptops (from &pound;510) and OptiPlex desktops (from &pound;545)</a> &mdash; guide prices, each machine fitted with a new 1TB Samsung 990 PRO SSD, set up with Windows 11, your data transferred, and covered by a 12-month return-to-base guarantee (five years on a support plan). Those are excellent machines for office and general business work &mdash; but we&rsquo;ll say it straight: a refurbished Latitude or OptiPlex is <em>not</em> a substitute for a workstation if your day is heavy CAD, 3D rendering or GPU compute. It may suit the second desk, the admin role, or the engineer who mostly runs email and spreadsheets.</p><p><strong>For a true workstation replacement, we order new Dell to your specification</strong> through our independent reseller account &mdash; sized for your actual workload, not the sales quarter. And when the old machine goes, our <a href=\"/secure-it-disposal/\">secure IT disposal</a> service makes sure project files and client data are properly destroyed, with the paperwork to prove it.</p>"
   }
